<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA M1 RISES 4.64 PCT, M2 UP 1.09 PCT IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA M1 RISES 4.64 PCT, M2 UP 1.09 PCT IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 1.334 trillion levs ($723.8 million) on August 1 from 1.275 trillion levs a week earlier, and M2 increased to 4.601 trillion levs from 4.551 trillion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 1.17 percent to 4.826 trillion levs in the week to August 1.</p>
<p>Conversion of foreign currency-denominated deposits into levs was made at the central bank fixing of 1,000 levs per mark for August 1 and July 25 and at 990.6 levs on June 27.</p>
<p>The lev was pegged at 1,000 per mark on July 1 under a currency board system, or a form of an IMF-prescribed fixed exchange rate mechanism aimed at restoring confidence in the lev and stabilising the economy.</p>
<p>The system requires levs in circulation to be fully matched by central bank foreign exchange reserves.</p>
